commit 69882b9f5d22763f7bd25b1cd2b0ca18444863ca
Author: Wayne <uvforce@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Sep 30 19:23:29 2026 +0800

    fix: group a turn whose anchor falls outside the first history page (#941)
    
    The session detail route serves the most recent 50 entries by default, so a
    turn longer than that page is delivered without its leading user message. The
    render loop treats every message before the first anchor as standalone and
    pushes it directly, which skips the process-details grouping for that turn:
    the whole turn renders flat, with no collapsible group, even though it has a
    final answer.
    
    Group the anchorless leading segment as well. findFinalAssistantIndex already
    scans back to userIdx + 1, so passing -1 covers index 0, and groupStartIdx
    keeps the render range and the group key pointing at the first loaded message.
    
    Co-authored-by: wayne.luo <wayne.luo@bybit.com>

